-- title:
--   Width-weighted adjointness of the two degeneracy Hecke correspondences
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $M, s, q'$ with $M, s$ nonzero, $s$ prime, $q'$ prime, $q' \ge 5$, $s \neq q'$ and $q' \nmid M$, and let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q'$ with decidable equality. Write $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldC k M`, the $k$-subfield of $k((q))$ generated by `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k M`, and $R =$ `charLDegeneracyRoof k M s`, the $k$-subfield generated by `jqModC k`, `jqNModC k M`, `jqNModC k s` and `jqNModC k (M * s)`; assume $R$ has principal divisors, i.e. every nonzero $f \in R$ admits a divisor of degree $0$ whose coefficient at each place $v$ is $v.\mathrm{ord}(f)$. Let $\alpha =$ `heckeAlphaC k M s` be the inclusion $F \hookrightarrow R$ and $\beta =$ `heckeBetaC k M s` the embedding induced by the substitution `qExpand k s`, both assumed to be integral ring maps (hypotheses `HeckeAlphaCIntegral`, `HeckeBetaCIntegral`). Then for all places $w_0, w'$ of $F$, writing $\mathrm{w}(\cdot)$ for `placeWidthChar q' M`, the quotient of `jWidthChar q'` of the evaluation of `jGeomGen k M` by `placeRamificationJ M`, viewed in $\mathbb{Z}$, one has $$\mathrm{w}(w')\cdot\bigl(\alpha_*\beta^*\,[w_0]\bigr)(w') = \mathrm{w}(w_0)\cdot\bigl(\beta_*\alpha^*\,[w']\bigr)(w_0),$$ where $[w]$ denotes the divisor `Finsupp.single w 1` and $\varphi_*\psi^*$ is `Divisor.correspondence` of the two embeddings, i.e. pullback along $\psi$ followed by pushforward along $\varphi$.
--
--   This is the statement that the two divisorial degeneracy (Hecke) correspondences $\alpha_*\beta^*$ and $\beta_*\alpha^*$ at prime level $s$ on the characteristic-$q'$ modular function field are adjoint to one another for the width-weighted pairing $\langle u,v\rangle = \sum_x \mathrm{w}(x)u(x)v(x)$ on places, with no condition relating $s$ and $M$ beyond $s \neq q'$, at the cost of restricting to $q' \ge 5$. It feeds the comparison of the Hecke-torsion in the component group of a supersingular-reduction datum with the corresponding quotient of the character lattice.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_placeWidthChar_mul_correspondence_heckeBetaC_heckeAlphaC_single_apply_eq_of_prime_of_five_le.lean

